※ pl4g-test: compile=ok opt=0,1 run=native,qemu exit=94 host=host.c
※ pl4g-test: args -shared

※ **Text a host answers is asked whether it is UTF-8**, as `⎕text` asks the
※ bytes it is handed: every `str` is well formed, and this is text coming in
※ from bytes nothing in the program wrote.  The declaration answers a string
※ and not a result, so bytes that are not one stop the program, with a status
※ of their own (94), before anything reads them.  `host.c` answers `61 C0 80`,
※ a nul written the long way after an `a`.

@[host("overlong")]
fn overlong() → str

@[visible, cdecl, impure]
fn run() → i32:
    let got: str = overlong()
    if got = "": 1i32 else: 2i32
